<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  NOT YET WIRED INTO THE XCODE PROJECT.

  ios/Runner.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj has no CODE_SIGN_ENTITLEMENTS setting,
  so this file is inert until someone opens the project on a Mac and sets it
  for the Debug, Release and Profile configurations. It is committed because
  the content is the part that is easy to get wrong, and because it records a
  blocker that is otherwise invisible from a Windows checkout.

  Why it is needed: since iOS 14, sending to a multicast address requires the
  com.apple.developer.networking.multicast entitlement. SSDP discovery is a
  UDP send to 239.255.255.250, so without this the scanner finds nothing at
  all on real iOS hardware. Bonjour/mDNS still works via NSBonjourServices,
  but Roku does not advertise over Bonjour, so a Roku would never appear.

  Apple grants this entitlement by request, not automatically:
  https://developer.apple.com/contact/request/networking-multicast
  Until it is granted and provisioning is regenerated, Manual IP is the only
  route to a device on iOS.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.developer.networking.multicast</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
